# Tech Blog Platform – Powered by Data Engineering Insights

## Purpose
This project is a personal blog platform designed to share knowledge, tutorials, and project experiences related to data engineering. It serves as a hub for showcasing hands-on work in areas like cloud data pipelines, ETL development, and modern data stack tools. The blog helps readers gain practical insights into real-world data engineering scenarios.

## Technologies Used
- **Frontend:** HTML, CSS, Markdown (if using static site generator)  
- **Backend (optional):** Flask or FastAPI (if dynamic)  
- **Hosting:** GitHub Pages or any static hosting platform  
- **Content:** Blog posts written in Markdown or HTML  
- **Version Control:** Git & GitHub

## How to Run It
1. **Clone the Repository:**  
   ```bash  
   git clone https://github.com/srividya980/blog-project  
   cd blog-project  
   ```

2. **Preview Blog Locally:**  
   If using a static site generator like Jekyll or Hugo:  
   ```bash  
   # For Jekyll (Ruby)
   bundle exec jekyll serve  
   ```

3. **Deploy Blog:**  
   - Push your changes to the main branch.  
   - If GitHub Pages is enabled, it will automatically publish your site.

